      <a href="#how-we-picked">How We Picked</a>
      <a href="#mistakes">Common Mistakes</a>
      <a href="#faq">FAQ</a>
    </TableOfContents>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="lede">
          The best dairy-free protein powder for most people is Vega Sport Premium Protein: about 30 g of plant protein per serving with no milk ingredients, and the brand states it is NSF Certified for Sport. On a budget, Orgain Organic Plant-Based is the everyday default, and if you want animal protein without dairy, Naked Egg White is the cleanest option. Just do not confuse dairy-free with lactose-free: a lactose-free whey isolate is still milk.
        </p>

        <QuickPicks products={PRODUCTS} />

        <div id="quick-comparison" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. Quick Comparison: The Best Dairy-Free Protein Powders
          </h2>

          <p>
            The short version: Vega Sport Premium Protein is the best dairy-free protein powder for most people who train, because it gives about 30 g of protein per serving and the brand states it is NSF Certified for Sport. Orgain is the budget default for everyday shakes, OWYN is the pick when you avoid several allergens at once, and Naked Egg is the answer if you want dairy-free animal protein rather than plants. Every pick below has no milk ingredient on the label at the time of writing, which is a stricter test than lactose-free. The table lines up the numbers, all read from labels or brand pages and varying by flavor.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
              <table class="w-full text-left">
                <thead class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-200">
